 website=part('Who this is for','Small service businesses that need a first website or a redesign that makes their offer and enquiry journey easier to understand. Also suitable for an agreed landing-page or brochure-site project.')+part('Deliverables you can agree before work starts','A page inventory, content responsibilities, responsive layouts, development, agreed booking or enquiry integration, technical search foundations, browser and accessibility checks, launch preparation and documented handover.')+listing(['Define the business audience and desired next action.','List each page, reusable component and integration.','Document title, heading, canonical and redirect requirements.','Agree acceptance criteria and ownership of accounts and files.'])+part('What is outside the starting scope','Ecommerce transactions, customer accounts, complex applications, extensive copywriting, photography and ongoing campaigns are separate work. Provider subscriptions, hosting and domains are included only when the proposal says so. A form is complete only when real delivery is tested.')+part('New website or redesign?','For a new website, start with the offer, audience and content. For a redesign, first inventory current URLs, useful content and working integrations; preserve or redirect them deliberately. Similar website-design and redesign questions belong in this service scope, rather than separate near-duplicate pages.')+part('Process and approval points','Discovery → written scope → content and layout approval → development preview → acceptance checks → approved launch → handover. Feedback rounds, dependencies and delivery dates are agreed in the proposal.')+part('Commercial approach','Request a tailored quote. Project fees follow the agreed pages, interactions, content and migration work. Changes receive a written cost and timing assessment before starting; recurring support is scoped separately.')+part('Evidence you can inspect','<a href="/work/olive-earth/">Olive & Earth</a> shows product browsing and a demonstration bag. <a href="/work/form-space/">Form / Space</a> shows project navigation and a demonstration consultation brief. These are original concepts, not client projects or proof of sales results. SiteSutra itself demonstrates static HTML, CSS and JavaScript delivery.')+part('Prepare a useful brief','Use the <a href="/guides/scope/">scope guide and downloadable brief</a>, <a href="/guides/redesign/">redesign inventory</a> and <a href="/guides/costs/">quote comparison guide</a> before we talk.')
 agency=part('Who this is for','Design, branding and marketing agencies with approved website work that needs additional development capacity. Start with one clearly defined deliverable, rather than an open-ended capacity commitment.')+part('White-label deliverables','Responsive implementation of agreed layouts, reusable components, approved integrations, staging previews, QA records, source delivery and handover under your agreed workflow.')+listing(['Your agency owns the client relationship. Client contact requires your agreement.','Agree design files, component states, content and acceptance criteria before estimating.','Record repository access, review milestones and who handles launch and client support.'])+part('Exclusions and boundaries','Client strategy, design changes, unscoped backend features, account administration and ongoing maintenance are separate unless agreed. Confidentiality and ownership are documented; no client material is added to SiteSutra’s portfolio without permission.')+part('Process','Share the brief and approved direction → agree a fixed-scope paid pilot → build in a review branch → agency QA and client approval → handover and approved release. Clarify who signs off each milestone.')+part('Commercial approach','Request a tailored quote for a pilot, project or defined support arrangement. Availability, communication overlap, revision rounds and change handling are confirmed in writing. No unsupported turnaround or capacity guarantees are offered.')+part('Review the implementation','Inspect the <a href="/demos/olive-earth/">retail demo</a>, <a href="/demos/form-space/">architecture demo</a> and their <a href="/work/">case studies</a>. They demonstrate original work, not confidential agency engagements. Static HTML, CSS and JavaScript are demonstrated here; other platform work requires a capability review against your brief.')+part('Plan the handover','Use the <a href="/guides/scope/">acceptance checklist</a> and <a href="/guides/platforms/">editing and maintenance demonstration</a> to define what your team needs after delivery.')
 design=part('Who this is for','Small businesses and agencies that need a coherent identity or a defined set of graphic assets for a website, presentation or campaign.')+part('Deliverables','Agree visual direction, logo refinement or development, colour and typography guidance, usage rules, named templates, export formats and editable source files. The asset list and revision rounds define the project.')+part('Exclusions','Brand research beyond the agreed brief, naming, trademark clearance, photography, illustration commissions, printing and unlimited revisions are separate. Font and image licences must be confirmed for the intended use.')+part('Process','Understand the audience → approve a direction → review concepts → refine the selected direction → approve named assets → deliver files and usage guidance.')+part('Commercial approach','Request a tailored quote around the asset list and approval rounds. Additional formats and ongoing design support are separately scoped.')+part('Relevant evidence','The <a href="/work/olive-earth/">retail concept</a> and <a href="/work/form-space/">architecture concept</a> demonstrate different palette, typography and layout treatments. They are fictional website identities, not commissioned branding programmes.')+part('Useful preparation','The <a href="/guides/scope/">scope guide</a> helps assign content and asset ownership. The <a href="/guides/costs/">cost guide</a> separates project work from recurring licences.')
 seo=part('Who this is for','Businesses and agencies with a website that needs a technical review, clearer service content or an agreed search-marketing plan. We prioritise fixes that support a real buyer journey.')+part('Audit and implementation deliverables','Agree crawl and indexability checks, URL inventory, descriptive metadata, headings, internal links, canonical and sitemap review, redirect recommendations, structured-data review and a prioritised implementation plan. Campaign or content work is specified separately.')+part('What is excluded','Guaranteed rankings, indexing, traffic, leads or AI recommendations are not deliverables. Paid media spend, large content programmes, link acquisition and third-party tools are separate; no purchased demand data is implied.')+part('Process','Confirm business goals and access → establish a documented baseline → review pages and technical evidence → prioritise work → implement approved changes → validate and report limitations.')+part('Commercial approach','Request a tailored quote for an audit, implementation project or ongoing review. Define URLs, access and reporting cadence before work starts; advertising spend is separate.')+part('Relevant evidence','These buyer guides and SiteSutra’s crawlable service pages demonstrate content structure and technical foundations. The <a href="/guides/redesign/">sample redirect map</a> is hypothetical, not a client audit. No commercial performance results are claimed.')+part('Three measures, three questions','Search visibility: impressions, clicks, queries and page coverage in verified search tools. AI citations: record dated prompts, assistant, cited URL and whether a citation actually appeared; this sample is not a market-wide visibility score. Qualified enquiries: record the source, service fit, goal, budget discussion and agreed next step after a real email or booking arrives. A booking-link click is not a confirmed enquiry.')+part('Candidate phrases need validation','Small-business website design, website redesign and white-label web development are relevance candidates. Validate them against real customer language and available search evidence; no search volume or difficulty has been established. Keep close variations on one useful service page.')+part('Related foundations','Read the <a href="/guides/redesign/">redesign guide</a> or discuss <a href="/services/website-development/">website design and development</a> when structural changes are needed.')
